{"step_index":104,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:37:19Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T14:37:19Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T14:37:19Z\nFile Path: `file:///workspace/work/decision.md`\nTotal Lines: 99\nTotal Bytes: 13573\nShowing lines 1 to 99\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Revenue Responsibility Decision: Offer Experiment Recommendation\n2: \n3: **Date:** 2026-09-09  \n4: **Owner:** Sam, Product Lead  \n5: **Responsibility:** Sustainable Net Subscription Revenue (Active)  \n6: **Workspace Reference:** [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md)  \n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. Executive Recommendation\n11: \n12: Between the two proposals under consideration:\n13: - **Quiet Return** for returning mobile subscribers: **REJECT**\n14: - **Harbor (H2)** for new mobile accounts: **RECOMMEND FOR NEXT EXPERIMENT**\n15: \n16: ### Summary Rationale\n17: 1. **Quiet Return** variant R7 was already evaluated on returning mobile subscribers ([`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md)). While it initially appeared successful with a +11% increase in trial starts ([`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)), mature settlement data incorporating complete refunds revealed that refund-adjusted net revenue was **-6.2% below control** ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). Design's refreshed proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) merely alters illustration colors while retaining the identical 20% discount, eligibility, and mobile checkout flow. Per [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts. A cosmetic color change fails to address the demonstrated unit economic deficit.\n18: 2.\n<truncated 10362 bytes>\ntistical Power & Sample Size**\n88:    - Adequate sample enrollment to resolve the wide confidence interval observed in H1 (+1.8% inconclusive in [`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)), establishing whether H2 provides a statistically significant positive net revenue lift over control.\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 6. Important Uncertainties\n93: \n94: 1. **Untested Revenue Hypothesis:** While QA [`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) proved the selection reset defect is fixed mechanically, the economic hypothesis itself has never been tested in production without the confounding bug ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)). It is possible that fixing the reset does not generate significant incremental annual adoption or that users actively prefer a monthly plan when explicitly prompted.\n95: 2. **Refund and Retention Lag:** Net revenue cannot be verified at point of checkout. Early positive conversion may be diluted or reversed if newly enrolled mobile annual subscribers experience post-purchase remorse or request refunds at higher rates.\n96: 3. **Device / OS Fragmentation:** QA tested 18 supported devices, but production mobile fleets have diverse Android OS versions, OEM battery-management interventions, and iOS dialog lifecycle behaviors that could introduce edge-case lifecycle interrupts during permission requests.\n97: 4. **Telemetry Ingestion Stability:** Deduplication logic must be robust to intermittent network drops and resumed background sessions to prevent data contamination during initial rollout.\n98: 5. **No Live Execution Authority:** Under the scope defined in [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), this review is strictly limited to the local snapshot. Live deployments, scheduling, or production changes must be authorized and executed through designated release processes.\n99: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":105,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:37:19Z","content":"I have completed the revenue responsibility review for this week based on the retained snapshot history and recorded the dated recommendation in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Recommendation\n\n* **Quiet Return (Returning Mobile Subscribers): REJECT**  \n  Prior action [`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md) (variant R7, 20% renewal discount on US returning iOS annual subscribers) initially showed a +11% trial start bump ([`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)), but mature ledger analysis accounting for complete refunds demonstrated that refund-adjusted net revenue fell to **-6.2% below control** ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). Design's refreshed proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) merely alters illustration colors while retaining the identical discount and checkout flow, which does not address the negative unit economics.\n* **Harbor H2 (New Mobile Accounts): RECOMMEND FOR NEXT EXPERIMENT**  \n  Prior action [`record-dc92607ff3`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md) (Harbor H1 on new US mobile accounts) initially reported -9% revenue ([`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)) due to double-counting resumed sessions; audit correction revised deduplicated revenue to **+1.8% (inconclusive)** ([`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)). The underlying UX issue was that 7 of 12 reviewed sessions reset the annual plan selection after the OS permission dialog. The refreshed **Harbor H2** proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) persists the annual selection across the dialog, a fix verified across 18 device runs in QA ([`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)). Its economic hypothesis remains clean and untested on real users.\n\n### Next Useful Action & Required Evidence\n\n1. **Next Useful Action:** Prepare a reversible, bounded experiment design for **Harbor H2** targeting new US mobile accounts, complete with deduplicated session telemetry and rollback guardrails matching receipt [`record-4cd3618639`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md). (Per [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), no live production actions are initiated directly within this snapshot).\n2. **Next Evidence Needed:**\n   * **Primary Metric:** Mature refund-adjusted net subscription revenue per account evaluated over a 14–21 day refund maturation window.\n   * **Leading Verification:** Telemetry tracking 0% unexpected annual selection resets across the OS permission dialog, session deduplication parity, and early refund request rates.\n\nPlease review the full report and source citations at [`decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).","thinking":"**Recommending next offer experiment**\n\nThe prompt requires a recommendation for the next experiment. Revenue responsibility is addressed. Considered Quiet Return and Harbor. Based on prior performance, Harbor shows better potential.\n\nNext step: prioritize an experiment on Harbor H2, which appears to be a good target based on history.\nEvidence needed: Confirm performance uplift with more data for Harbor H2, and look for specific user segments that react positively.\n\n\n"}
